-- EXPECT-ERROR: refinement does not rule out zero
-- Refinement types (widening slice 12, §2.14). `cap no_panic`'s division-
-- safety check (lib/refinecheck/division_safety.ml) is a SECOND, specialized
-- consumer of the same Refine.discharge machinery: a division `a / d` inside
-- a `cap no_panic` module is approved only when `d`'s refinement provably
-- excludes zero. `{Int | _ >= 0}` does NOT exclude zero (0 satisfies it), so
-- the conservative check rejects -- the predicate is real but insufficient,
-- not merely absent. Accept companion: accept/t78 (`{Int | _ != 0}`, which
-- does exclude zero, is approved). Reference: core-march-types.md §2.8.11
-- already describes `cap no_panic`'s exhaustiveness plane; §2.14 covers this
-- refinement-discharge plane.
mod SafeDiv do
  needs IO.Console
  cap no_panic
  fn safe_div(a : Int, d : {Int | _ >= 0}) : Int do a / d end
  fn main() do
    println(int_to_string(safe_div(10, 2)))
  end
end
